561		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
562			<section aria-label="Introduction">
563				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
564				<p>
565					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
566					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
567				</p>
568				<p>
569					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
570					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
571				</p>
572			</section>
573	
574			<section aria-labelledby="features">
575				<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
576				<ul>
577					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
578					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
579					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
580					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
581					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
582					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
583				</ul>
584			</section>
585	
586			<section aria-labelledby="examples">
587				<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
588				<article class="card">
589					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
590					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
591					<a class="button" href="#resources">Learn more<span class="visually-hidden"> about accessibility resources</span></a>
592				</article>
593	
594				<article class="card">
595					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
596					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. All interactive elements include visible focus indicators and proper ARIA labels.</p>
597					<p><strong>Keyboard navigation:</strong> Use <kbd>Tab</kbd> to move forward, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd> to move backward, and <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd> to activate.</p>
598				</article>
599	
600				<article class="card">
601					<h3>Accessible Form</h3>
602					<form id="contact-form" novalidate>
603						<p class="form-hint">Fields marked * are required.</p>
604						<div class="field">
605							<label for="email">Email <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
606							<input type="email" id="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="none" required aria-describedby="email-help">
607							<span id="email-error" class="error-message"></span>
608							<small id="email-help" class="form-hint">For example, name@example.com</small>
609						</div>
610						<div class="field">
611							<label for="message">Message</label>
612							<textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" maxlength="2000" aria-describedby="message-help"></textarea>
613							<small id="message-help" class="form-hint">Up to 2,000 characters. <span id="message-count">2,000</span> remaining.</small>
614						</div>
615						<button type="submit">Send message</button>
616						<p id="form-status" role="status"></p>
617					</form>
618				</article>
